title: Route1Viewing
tags: cutscene
---
<<declare $samantha_name = "_Samantha">>
<<declare $r1_viewing_opening = "">>
<<declare $r1_viewing_why = "">>
<<declare $r1_viewing_question = "">>
// Landing. He knocked on 3B; the door across the hall opens instead.
<<walk Player PlayerKnock>>
<<face Player up>>
<<open_door Door3A>>
<<show Samantha>>
<<walk Samantha SamanthaOut>>
<<face Samantha Player>>
<<face Player Samantha>>
{$samantha_name}: Nobody's in there. That's sort of the point.
You: Oh. Sorry. I'm here for the viewing.
{$samantha_name}: I know. You're six minutes early.
{$samantha_name}: Keen or nervous?
-> Keen. I really need a place.
    <<set $r1_viewing_opening to "keen">>
    {$samantha_name}: Honest. That's a terrible way to start a negotiation.
    {$samantha_name}: I'll pretend I didn't hear it.
-> Nervous, if I'm honest.
    <<set $r1_viewing_opening to "nervous">>
    {$samantha_name}: Cute. Most people pretend they aren't.
-> Just punctual.
    <<set $r1_viewing_opening to "punctual">>
    {$samantha_name}: Mm. You're going a little red, but sure.
// She turns back to her open door for the keys (assumes 3A is south of her).
<<face Samantha down>>
{$samantha_name}: My father owns the building. He's away this week, so you get me instead.
<<face Samantha Player>>
<<set $samantha_name to "Samantha">>
{$samantha_name}: Samantha. That's my door. Whoever takes this flat gets me as a neighbour, too.
You: Nice to meet you, I'm-
{$samantha_name}: I know who you are. You sent an application. With a photo.
{$samantha_name}: Brave choice, the photo.
// She unlocks 3B and stays in the doorway.
<<walk Samantha SamanthaTo3B>>
<<face Samantha up>>
<<open_door Door3B>>
<<face Samantha Player>>
<<face Player Samantha>>
{$samantha_name}: Shoes off, please.
You: House rule?
{$samantha_name}: My rule. My father doesn't care.
{$samantha_name}: Interesting socks.
// Kitchen.
<<walk Samantha SamanthaToKitchen no_wait>>
<<walk Player PlayerToKitchen>>
<<await_walks>>
<<face Samantha Player>>
<<face Player Samantha>>
{$samantha_name}: Kitchen. The stove works. The oven works if you ask it nicely.
{$samantha_name}: The last tenant never asked nicely.
You: What happened to him?
{$samantha_name}: He moved out. People do.
{$samantha_name}: So. You just finished?
You: Last month. This would be my first flat.
{$samantha_name}: I can tell. You're looking at the sockets like they might bite.
{$samantha_name}: How old are you, anyway?
You: Old enough to sign a lease.
{$samantha_name}: Barely, by the look of you. I'm twenty-five, I've signed four.
// Bedroom.
<<walk Samantha SamanthaToBedroom no_wait>>
<<walk Player PlayerToBedroom>>
<<await_walks>>
<<face Samantha Player>>
<<face Player Samantha>>
{$samantha_name}: Bedroom. The bed's not included. The last tenant took it. Sentimental, I suppose.
// The window. Both look out (assumes the window is on the north wall).
<<walk Samantha SamanthaToWindow no_wait>>
<<walk Player PlayerToWindow>>
<<await_walks>>
<<face Samantha up>>
<<face Player up>>
{$samantha_name}: And this is the part I always save for last.
{$samantha_name}: Tram stop on the corner. Bakery opens at six. You'll hate it for a week, then you'll love it.
<<face Samantha Player>>
<<face Player Samantha>>
{$samantha_name}: So. Why this one?
-> The light. It's nice in here.
    <<set $r1_viewing_why to "light">>
    {$samantha_name}: It is. I'll tell my father. He'll act like he built the sun.
-> Honestly? It's the one I can afford.
    <<set $r1_viewing_why to "money">>
    {$samantha_name}: Practical. He'd like that. I find it a little boring.
    {$samantha_name}: Lucky for you, he's not the one deciding.
-> It's the first place that wrote back.
    <<set $r1_viewing_why to "first">>
    {$samantha_name}: Wow. You really know how to make someone feel special.
    {$samantha_name}: I'll try not to take it personally.
// Back on the landing. She locks up.
<<walk Samantha SamanthaToLanding no_wait>>
<<walk Player PlayerToLanding>>
<<await_walks>>
<<face Samantha up>>
<<close_door Door3B>>
<<face Samantha Player>>
<<face Player Samantha>>
{$samantha_name}: Anything you want to ask me?
-> When will I hear back?
    <<set $r1_viewing_question to "when">>
    {$samantha_name}: When I've decided.
    You: Not your father?
    {$samantha_name}: He signs whatever I hand him.
-> Are the neighbours quiet?
    <<set $r1_viewing_question to "neighbours">>
    {$samantha_name}: The man downstairs, very.
    {$samantha_name}: Across the hall... depends on the night.
-> No, I think I've seen everything.
    <<set $r1_viewing_question to "none">>
    {$samantha_name}: You haven't. But it's enough for one day.
{$samantha_name}: There are two more viewings this week.
{$samantha_name}: Both of them wore matching socks.
{$samantha_name}: I'll let you know.
// She goes back through her own door.
<<walk Samantha SamanthaHome>>
<<hide Samantha>>
<<close_door Door3A>>
// Time skip to moving day (route1_movein.yarn).
<<fade_out>>
<<next_scene Route1MoveIn>>
===
